==Latin==

===Etymology===
From {{der|la|ine-pro|*péth₂eti||to fall; fly}}. Cognates include {{cog|grc|πέτομαι||I fly}}, {{cog|sa|पतति|tr=pátati|sc=Deva}}, Avestan {{cog|ae|𐬞𐬀𐬙𐬀𐬌𐬙𐬌|tr=pataiti}} and {{cog|xcl|թիռ||flight, desire}}. See English {{m|en|feather}}, {{m|en|pen}} for more.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|petō}}

===Verb===
{{la-verb|petō|petere|petīvī|perf2=petīī|petītum|conj=3}}

# I [[ask]], [[beg]], [[request]].
# I [[make for]] (somewhere).
# I [[seek]], [[aim]] at, [[desire]].
#: ''Auxilium deorum '''peto'''.''
#:: '''I am seeking''' the help of the gods.
#: ''Altiora '''peto'''.''
#:: '''I seek''' higher things.
# I [[beg]], [[beseech]].
# I [[attack]].
#: '''''Petere''' aliquem hasta.''
#:: To '''attack''' someone with a spear.
# {{lb|la|ecclesiastical}} To [[missionize]] or [[proselytize]] among the people of a place.
#: ''Peter Romam Marcus Alexandriam '''petit'''''.
#:: Peter proselytizes in Rome; Mark, in Alexandria. (Bede, ''Chronica Minor'')

====Inflection====
